WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:09.692
Bobby loves to read books. He reads every chance he gets.

2
00:00:09.693 --> 00:00:14.796
He reads fiction and nonfiction. He reads history and biography.

3
00:00:14.797 --> 00:00:18.126
Bobby also loves mystery and science fiction.

4
00:00:18.127 --> 00:00:23.797
But Bobby's favorite books are about science, especially plants.

5
00:00:23.798 --> 00:00:27.115
All of the kids in school call Bobby bookworm.

6
00:00:27.116 --> 00:00:30.617
But they don't always mean it in a nice way.

7
00:00:30.618 --> 00:00:34.510
A lot of kids tease Bobby and call him bad names.

8
00:00:34.511 --> 00:00:37.637
But Bobby tries to ignore them.

9
00:00:37.638 --> 00:00:42.356
One day Bobby's class went on a field trip to Rockbridge Park.

10
00:00:42.357 --> 00:00:45.388
Bobby was in a group with five other students.

11
00:00:45.389 --> 00:00:50.444
One of them, named Kyle, made fun of Bobby all the time.

12
00:00:50.445 --> 00:00:54.952
"Where's your book, bookworm?" Kyle said.

13
00:00:54.953 --> 00:01:00.052
"Class, stay in your groups, please!" Mrs. Murphy called.

14
00:01:00.053 --> 00:01:05.412
The class followed Mrs. Murphy and the park ranger as they walked into the forest.

15
00:01:05.413 --> 00:01:09.510
The ranger explained about the different types of trees and plants.

16
00:01:09.511 --> 00:01:12.958
Suddenly Bobby felt someone grab his bag.

17
00:01:12.959 --> 00:01:18.076
"Hey, bookworm! What's this?" teased Kyle.

18
00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:21.928
"Give me back my book!" said Bobby.

19
00:01:21.929 --> 00:01:25.515
"Come and get it!" said the boys.

20
00:01:25.516 --> 00:01:29.640
Bobby wanted his book, so he ran after Kyle and Frank.

21
00:01:29.641 --> 00:01:33.345
Kyle and Frank ran deeper and deeper into the woods.

22
00:01:33.346 --> 00:01:35.526
Bobby finally caught up with them.

23
00:01:35.527 --> 00:01:39.494
"Give me back my book!" demanded Bobby.

24
00:01:39.495 --> 00:01:45.001
"My pleasure!" said Kyle. He threw the book on the ground.

25
00:01:45.002 --> 00:01:48.513
"Let's get out of here," said Frank.

26
00:01:48.514 --> 00:01:51.946
"Which way do we go?" asked Kyle.

27
00:01:51.947 --> 00:01:56.765
"Uh, Kyle, I think we're lost," said Frank.

28
00:01:56.766 --> 00:02:00.713
"I'm getting cold," said Kyle.

29
00:02:00.714 --> 00:02:03.887
"I'm hungry," Frank whined.

30
00:02:03.888 --> 00:02:09.999
"Me too. And my feet are killing me," complained Kyle.

31
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.438
Bobby quietly took out some candy. He gave it to Frank and Kyle.

32
00:02:15.439 --> 00:02:21.363
"Hey, thanks, bookworm," said the boys.

33
00:02:21.364 --> 00:02:26.810
"Hey, look! Let's eat those berries!" said Kyle.

34
00:02:26.811 --> 00:02:32.591
"No! Don't eat those! They're poisonous!" shouted Bobby.

35
00:02:32.592 --> 00:02:34.598
"That's the red baneberry.

36
00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:38.074
The flower petals are white and it smells like a rose.

37
00:02:38.075 --> 00:02:42.583
But the berries and roots are poisonous," said Bobby.

38
00:02:42.584 --> 00:02:46.723
The three boys walked and walked. They looked for the rest of the class.

39
00:02:46.724 --> 00:02:49.765
"I'm getting tired," cried Frank.

40
00:02:49.766 --> 00:02:53.579
"Let's sit here and rest," said Kyle.

41
00:02:53.580 --> 00:03:00.160
"Wait! Don't sit there!" shouted Bobby. "That's poison ivy!"

42
00:03:00.161 --> 00:03:05.171
"Gosh, how do you know so much about plants?" asked Frank.

43
00:03:05.172 --> 00:03:08.932
"I read about them in books," answered Bobby.

44
00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:13.111
"Come on, I'll show you some other poisonous plants and berries."

45
00:03:13.112 --> 00:03:15.832
Bobby led the two boys along the path.

46
00:03:15.833 --> 00:03:19.259
They stopped in front of bushes and trees.

47
00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.456
Bobby explained about the different flowers and plants.

48
00:03:22.457 --> 00:03:25.719
The boys were very interested in what they saw.

49
00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.770
Soon they forgot they were lost!

50
00:03:28.771 --> 00:03:33.383
"Wow! You're so smart," said Kyle.

51
00:03:33.384 --> 00:03:37.755
"I wish I knew as much as you do," said Frank.

52
00:03:37.756 --> 00:03:41.421
"It's not because I'm smarter than you," said Bobby.

53
00:03:41.422 --> 00:03:44.612
"It's because I read about plants in books."

54
00:03:44.613 --> 00:03:50.842
Suddenly they heard a familiar voice. "Kyle! Frank! Bobby!"

55
00:03:50.843 --> 00:03:54.858
It was Mrs. Murphy. She was with the park ranger.

56
00:03:54.859 --> 00:03:59.024
"Are you okay?" asked Mrs. Murphy.

57
00:03:59.025 --> 00:04:06.375
"We were very worried because the forest has many dangers and poisonous plants!" said the park ranger.

58
00:04:06.376 --> 00:04:15.670
"Bookworm . . . I mean, Bobby is an expert on plants, so we were okay," said Kyle.

59
00:04:15.671 --> 00:04:19.091
"Well, you boys are in big trouble!

60
00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:25.234
You will go to the library and do research on all the poisonous plants in North America.

61
00:04:25.235 --> 00:04:30.005
Then you will present it to the class," said Mrs. Murphy.

62
00:04:30.006 --> 00:04:33.449
The three boys looked at each other and smiled.

63
00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:37.566
"What are you smiling about?" asked Mrs. Murphy.

64
00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:43.175
"Nothing, Mrs. Murphy. We're sorry!" the boys said together.

65
00:04:43.176 --> 00:04:48.042
From then on, every Saturday, the three friends went to the library.

66
00:04:48.043 --> 00:04:52.316
Kyle and Frank soon realized why Bobby loved to read so much.

67
00:04:52.317 --> 00:04:58.309
They decided to start a club. They called it The Bookworm Club.
